  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J7", "J11"],
      "pins": ["J7.1", "J11.1"],
      "nets": ["NET0004"],
      "observed": "On the EthernetAndPower sheet the label NET0004 is attached to pin 1 (TD+) of the RJ45 jack J7 and also to pin 1 (centre/positive) of the DC barrel jack J11. NET0004 is the battery/USB/adapter input rail on this sheet (it is the node fed by the barrel-jack centre pin and by the battery feed diode U9 and going on to C10/IC2 VIN), while the other three J7 data pins carry NET0007 / NET0013 / NET0027, which are the nets that actually run to the SKW92A (U10) WAN-port pins on the SkylabModule sheet.",
      "expected": "The four data pins of J7 must connect only to the SKW92A WAN-port Ethernet nets (NET0007/NET0041/NET0013/NET0027); the DC-input / battery rail must not be connected to the Ethernet jack.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EthernetAndPower sheet: wire from J7 pin 1 carries global label NET0004; wire from J11 pin 1 carries global label NET0004, with note '2 and 3 are shorted with no plug / 1 is center, center is positive'"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "DC barrel jack (J4, \"Barrel_Jack_Switch\"): ... Netlist: J4.1→BAT+ (center/positive), J4.2→GND (sleeve), J4.3→BAT-."}
      ],
      "impact": "The Ethernet TD+ line is shorted to the battery/USB/DC power rail, so the WAN port cannot work and the rail is loaded by the RJ45 magnetics; at the same time one Ethernet pair of the SKW92A (the net that should reach J7 pin 1) is left unconnected at the jack.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The only clear deviation found is on the EthernetAndPower sheet, where the power/battery rail net NET0004 is also attached to pin 1 of the RJ45 jack J7, bridging the DC/battery input rail with the Ethernet interface instead of routing that pin to the SKW92A WAN port; the rest of the power, reset, UART, keyboard, SD and EPD connections read as described in the specification."
}

